	(text "AUDIO BANDWIDTH / FILTER AUDIT\nOnly two reactive parts sit in the signal path.  The rest of\nthe chain is resistive, and the MAX97220 DirectDrive output\nis ground-referenced, so J1 needs no output cap and has none.\n\n1) Reconstruction LP: R16/R17 470R + C20/C21 2.2nF, loaded\n   by VR1 10k.   R = 470||10k = 449R\n   fc = 1/(2*pi*449*2.2n) = 161 kHz  ->  -0.07 dB @ 20 kHz\n\n2) Input coupling HP: C1/C4 1uF into R_IN 47k\n   fc = 1/(2*pi*47k*1u) = 3.4 Hz  ->  -0.12 dB @ 20 Hz\n   C2/C3 are the matching IN+ legs and are 1uF too --\n   both halves must track or LF CMRR degrades.\n\nDeviation over the audible band:\n   20 Hz -0.12 | 50 Hz -0.02 | 1 kHz 0.00 | 20 kHz -0.07 dB\n\nR_IN was 10k, putting this corner at 33.9 Hz (-5.87 dB at\n20 Hz).  Raising it to 47k is what fixed the bass rolloff.\nC1-C4 went 0.47uF -> 1uF: flatter, and it halves the signal\nacross the ceramic at 20 Hz (34% -> 17%), so less X7R\ndistortion down low.  Use X7R or better, never Y5V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 13.97 113.03 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "4936456b-f020-4e00-a5b4-096b6c5b2b2d")
	)
	(text "DAC"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
